=\"lex-cite-scope\">1.3</span> </span> <span class=\"lex-cite-date\">(iv B. C.)</span>; also, <b class=\"lex-tr\">concubine,</b> <span class=\"lex-cite\"> <span class=\"lex-cite-author\">Il.</span> <span class=\"lex-cite-scope\">24.497</span> </span>. </div> <div class=\"lex-sense\" data-level=\"2\"><span class=\"lex-n\">III</span> <b class=\"lex-tr\">mortal woman,</b> opp.<b class=\"lex-tr\">goddess,</b> <span class=\"lex-cite\"> <span class=\"lex-cite-scope\">14.315</span> </span>, <span class=\"lex-cite\"> <span class=\"lex-cite-author\">Od.</span> <span class=\"lex-cite-scope\">10.228</span> </span>, etc. </div> <div class=\"lex-sense\" data-level=\"2\"><span class=\"lex-n\">IV</span> <b class=\"lex-tr\">female, mate</b> of animals, <span class=\"lex-cite\"> <span class=\"lex-cite-author\">Arist.</span> <cite class=\"lex-cite-title\">Pol.</cite> <span class=\"lex-cite-scope\">1262a22</span> </span> (dub. sens.), <span class=\"lex-cite\"> <span class=\"lex-cite-author\">Xenarch.</span> <span class=\"lex-cite-scope\">14</span> </span>, etc.— Not to be taken as <span class=\"lex-gram\">Adj.</span> in <span class=\"gk\">γυναῖκα θήσατο μαζόν</span> <span class=\"lex-cite\"> <span class=\"lex-cite-author\">Il.</span> <span class=\"lex-cite-scope\">24.58</span> </span>. (Cf. Ved. <b class=\"lex-tr\">gnā-</b> (freq. disyll.), Skt. <b class=\"lex-tr\">janis.</b>)</div></div>"}